WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.767
The fine-tune to deploy pipeline.

2
00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.765
Fine-tuning is not a notebook.

3
00:00:04.765 --> 00:00:07.200
It is a pipeline with a gate in the middle.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.967
Here is the sentence that signals seniority.

5
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:14.000
The eval gate decides, not the training loss.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.767
Nothing merges, quantizes, or ships unless it beats the base model on the golden set.

7
00:00:20.967 --> 00:00:22.767
Here is the pipeline end to end.

8
00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.286
It starts with data.

9
00:00:24.286 --> 00:00:27.700
The golden set is carved out first, before any training.

10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.567
Then we train, usually with a LoRA adapter.

11
00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:31.628
Now the gate.

12
00:00:31.628 --> 00:00:34.733
Does the tuned model beat the base on the golden set?

13
00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:37.733
Only if it passes do we merge and quantize.

14
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.167
And then we deploy.

15
00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.733
Before building any of this, pick the right tool.

16
00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.833
Try prompting first, always.

17
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.900
Facts that change belong in RAG.

18
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.433
Fine-tune for style, format and domain reflexes.

19
00:00:51.633 --> 00:00:53.867
Another tradeoff is adapter strategy.

20
00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.433
One merged model is simple to serve.

21
00:00:56.733 --> 00:01:00.611
Or keep one adapter per tenant and hot-swap them at inference.

22
00:01:00.611 --> 00:01:02.800
That wins for many small customers.

23
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.376
Two classic mistakes.

24
00:01:05.376 --> 00:01:13.567
Catastrophic forgetting: a narrow fine-tune degrades general ability, and contamination, where test data leaks into training.

25
00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:19.633
The fix: mix in general data, evaluate broadly, and never let the golden set touch training.

26
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:22.300
Picture this in practice.

27
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.500
The training loss keeps falling and everyone is happy.

28
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.633
But on the golden set, the model loses to the base.

29
00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:29.974
So nothing ships.

30
00:01:29.974 --> 00:01:31.933
We fix the data and train again.

31
00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:33.909
Let's recap.

32
00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:36.367
Fine-tuning is a pipeline with a gate.

33
00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.967
The golden set decides, not the loss.

34
00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.900
Prompt first, RAG for facts, tune for style.

35
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.188
And never let the golden set touch training.

36
00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:47.700
Next up: the evals-first LLMOps loop.
